{"name":"Cardamom Fragrance","hex":"#d7e2bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cardamom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An herb, native to India (Elettaria cardamomum).","Seed of Elettaria cardamomum, used as a medicine and spice, especially in curry powder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardamom"},{"term":"fragrance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pleasant smell or odour.","A perfume."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply a fragrance to; to perfume."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardamom","blocks":[{"text":"Cardamom, sometimes cardamon or cardamum, is a spice made from the seeds of several plants in the genera Elettaria and Amomum in the family Zingiberaceae. Both genera are native to the Indian subcontinent and Indonesia. They are recognized by their small seed pods: triangular in cross-section and spindle-shaped, with a thin, papery outer shell and small, black seeds; Elettaria pods are light green and smaller, while Amomum pods are dark brown and larger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/02017_0119_Kardamom%2C_Winter_in_den_Beskiden.jpg/330px-02017_0119_Kardamom%2C_Winter_in_den_Beskiden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardamom","wikidata":"Q14625808"},{"title":"Fragrance compound","blocks":[{"text":"A fragrance compound is a chemical compound with a pleasant odor. Fragrances affect only the sense of smell, whereas flavors can affect both the sense of taste and smell. Fragrances are often mixtures of individual fragrance compounds. Although many fragrances are derived from natural sources, many are synthetic. Fragrances are widely used in cosmetics and are the basis for a large industry."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fragrance_compound","wikidata":"Q2151963"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or